# StreamCaverns LOD-churn fly-through (volumetric-sectors M0 seam soak).
# One pose per RENDERED frame: eye_x eye_y eye_z target_x target_y target_z
#
# WHY THIS PATH IS HORIZONTAL. M0 is still the XZ-columnar grid: the streaming
# anchor is 2-D (Coordinator::submit_anchor takes (x, z) and discards camera
# Y) and every band radius is a horizontal distance. Descending a shaft moves
# the anchor NOT AT ALL, so no tile splits, no tile merges, and no cross-level
# face pair is ever created -- the welder would sit at zero and the run would
# 'pass' having tested nothing. Y becomes a streaming axis in M3, not here.
#
# So the measurement is lateral speed. StreamCaverns' nested bands are at
# 160/384/832/1600/2624/4096 m (StreamCaverns.js), and the whole band structure
# translates with the anchor, so every metre of horizontal travel sweeps every
# level boundary by a metre. 3.0 m/pose keeps them sweeping continuously.
#
# Phases:
#   0- 799  +X traverse, 2400 m at 3.0 m/pose
#   800- 899  yaw +X -> +Z, anchor STILL (control: expect no churn)
#   900-1699  +Z traverse, 2400 m at 3.0 m/pose
#  1700-1999  diagonal home, 2160 m at 7.2 m/pose (outruns the streamer on purpose)
#  2000-2199  vertical descent to -120 m (CONTROL: 2-D anchor, expect no new pairs)
#
# Camera holds y=230 (the plateau tops out near 151 m) and looks 300 m ahead,
# 200 m down, so the tiles streaming in ahead of the anchor are the ones drawn.
-1200.000 230.000 0.000 -900.000 30.000 0.000
